\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces ParetoBandit adaptation dynamics across a three-phase cost scenario: normal pricing $\to $ Gemini price drop (step\nonbreakingspace 609) $\to $ price restored (step\nonbreakingspace 1217). $K{=}3$, 20\nonbreakingspace seeds, 95\% bootstrap CI. \textbf  {(a)}\nonbreakingspace Gemini-Pro selection fraction: when Gemini becomes nearly free, the tight budget surges to ${\sim }70\%$ Gemini adoption while the unconstrained baseline reaches ${\sim }60\%$---the pacer exploits the price drop more aggressively at tight budgets because the residual $\lambda _t$ favours the now-cheapest arm. \textbf  {(b)}\nonbreakingspace Windowed mean reward (trailing 50\nonbreakingspace steps): quality lifts during the price drop track the Gemini adoption in\nonbreakingspace (a), then return to Phase\nonbreakingspace 1 levels after price restoration. \textbf  {(c)}\nonbreakingspace Windowed average cost per request; dotted lines mark budget targets. All three regimes recover budget compliance in Phase\nonbreakingspace 3. See Table\nonbreakingspace \ref {tab:budget_compliance} for quantitative comparisons.}}{14}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:adaptation_dynamics}{{4}{14}{ParetoBandit adaptation dynamics across a three-phase cost scenario: normal pricing $\to $ Gemini price drop (step~609) $\to $ price restored (step~1217). $K{=}3$, 20~seeds, 95\% bootstrap CI. \textbf {(a)}~Gemini-Pro selection fraction: when Gemini becomes nearly free, the tight budget surges to ${\sim }70\%$ Gemini adoption while the unconstrained baseline reaches ${\sim }60\%$---the pacer exploits the price drop more aggressively at tight budgets because the residual $\lambda _t$ favours the now-cheapest arm. \textbf {(b)}~Windowed mean reward (trailing 50~steps): quality lifts during the price drop track the Gemini adoption in~(a), then return to Phase~1 levels after price restoration. \textbf {(c)}~Windowed average cost per request; dotted lines mark budget targets. All three regimes recover budget compliance in Phase~3. See Table~\ref {tab:budget_compliance} for quantitative comparisons}{figure.caption.31}{}}
