\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Model onboarding under budget constraints ($K{=}3 \to K{=}4$, 20\nonbreakingspace seeds, 95\% bootstrap CI). A $K{=}3$ router onboards Gemini-2.5-Flash via \texttt  {register\_model()} (dashed vertical line) with no warmup priors. \textbf  {(a)}\nonbreakingspace Flash adoption trajectory: the windowed selection fraction rises from zero and stabilises within ${\sim }230$ steps across all budget tiers. Loose budgets reach ${\sim }38$\% Flash share; tight budgets plateau at ${\sim }14$\%. \textbf  {(b)}\nonbreakingspace Full arm composition under the moderate budget: Flash primarily displaces Mistral-Large ($-22.9$\,pp), taking over the mid-cost quality niche at lower cost. \textbf  {(c)}\nonbreakingspace Cost compliance on log scale: ParetoBandit (solid) tracks each budget target (dotted) within ${\sim }2$\% across the full trajectory, while the Fixed Policy (dashed grey) exceeds all targets by 2--14$\times $.}}{18}{figure.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:model_onboarding}{{6}{18}{Model onboarding under budget constraints ($K{=}3 \to K{=}4$, 20~seeds, 95\% bootstrap CI). A $K{=}3$ router onboards Gemini-2.5-Flash via \texttt {register\_model()} (dashed vertical line) with no warmup priors. \textbf {(a)}~Flash adoption trajectory: the windowed selection fraction rises from zero and stabilises within ${\sim }230$ steps across all budget tiers. Loose budgets reach ${\sim }38$\% Flash share; tight budgets plateau at ${\sim }14$\%. \textbf {(b)}~Full arm composition under the moderate budget: Flash primarily displaces Mistral-Large ($-22.9$\,pp), taking over the mid-cost quality niche at lower cost. \textbf {(c)}~Cost compliance on log scale: ParetoBandit (solid) tracks each budget target (dotted) within ${\sim }2$\% across the full trajectory, while the Fixed Policy (dashed grey) exceeds all targets by 2--14$\times $}{figure.caption.49}{}}
